---
import StandardLayout from '@/layouts/StandardLayout.astro';
import Article from '@/components/article/Article';
import Hero from '@/images/about/hero.jpg';
import Article1 from '@/images/about/article1.png';
import Article2 from '@/images/about/article2.png';
import Article3 from '@/images/about/article3.png';
import Article4 from '@/images/about/article4.png';
import bowtie from '@/images/goobers/bowtie.svg';
import eyes from '@/images/goobers/eyes.svg';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import ArticleSection from '@/components/article/ArticleSection';
import Button from '@/components/button';
---
<StandardLayout
    title="About Us"
    description="We are Ro/Box. We make robotics and STEM education affordable, accessible, and fun for everyone."
>
    <div class="hero h-100 w-full relative">
        <Image src={Hero} alt="A Ro/Box sitting on a stone ledge, with sunlit leaves out of focus behind it" class="h-full object-cover w-full z-0 absolute object-right" width={Hero.width} height={Hero.height}/>
        <div class="about-us bg-green box-shadow z-10 relative lg:w-100 lg:top-1/3 top-50 bottom-0 w-60 rounded-r-2xl lg:pb-90 ">
            <h1 class="p-12">
                About Us
            </h1>
            <div class="images absolute bottom-12 left-12 right-12 hidden lg:flex items-end justify-between" aria-hidden="true">
                <!-- Original sizes rather than its 30%/50% of the title block:
                     ours is narrower, so the percentages rendered undersized. -->
                <img src={bowtie.src} alt="" class="mb-16 w-[108px]" />
                <img src={eyes.src} alt="" class="eyes w-[180px]" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="w-full lg:pl-100 flex flex-col justify-center my-20">
        <h1 class="text-center text-5xl">
            We are Ro/Box.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-center text-2xl mt-8 mx-20 leading-[150%]">
            We make robotics and STEM education affordable, accessible, and fun for everyone.
        </p>
    </div>
    <Article>
        <ArticleSection id="our-mission" direction="LTR" className='flex-col'>
            <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2 flex flex-col justify-center gap-6">
                <h1 class="text-left mb-8">
                    Our Mission
                </h1>
                <h2 class="text-left text-3xl font-semibold mb-4">
                    STEM education should be for everyone.
                </h2>
                <p class="text-left text-xl leading-[150%]">
                    At Ro/Box, our mission is to make hands-on engineering and coding education more affordable and accessible to all students, regardless of their background or resources. We are greatly motivated by the opportunities of STEM and robotics, and believe the future belongs to creators, problem-solvers, and innovators. By breaking down the financial barriers to robotics, we hope to open the door for everyone to experience the opportunities and love for robotics we have.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2 h-full flex justify-center items-center"> 
                <Image src={Article1} alt="A Ro/Box on a wooden desk beside a stack of school books" class="rounded-lg max-w-full max-h-full w-full object-cover object-center" width={Article1.width} height={Article1.height}/>
            </div>
        </ArticleSection>
        <ArticleSection id="our-story" direction="RTL" className='flex-col'>
            <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2 flex flex-col justify-center gap-6">
                <h1 class="text-left mb-8">
                    Our Story
                </h1>
                <p class="text-left text-xl leading-[150%]">
                    Ro/Box began with <a href="https://madebyyuma.com/" target="_blank">Yuma Soerianto</a> as a winning project for the <a href="https://www.risefortheworld.org/winners/hadriel-yuma-soerianto/" target="_blank">Rise Challenge</a>, an initiative that selects 100 young people globally to support their high-impact ideas. His project focused on tackling the high cost of robotics in STEM education, motivated by the high prices of robotics kits at his school's robotics club. These high prices pose serious challenges for schools and limit access to STEM learning for countless students.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="w-full h-full lg:w-1/2 flex justify-center items-center"> 
                <Image src={Article2} alt="An early Ro/Box prototype built from a milk carton, following a black line taped to the floor" class="rounded-lg max-w-full max-h-full w-full object-cover object-center" width={Article2.width} height={Article2.height}/>
            </div>
        </ArticleSection>
        <ArticleSection direction="LTR" className='flex-col'>
            <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2 flex flex-col justify-center gap-6">
                <p class="text-left text-xl leading-[150%]">
                    After the project won the Rise Challenge, Yuma realised that Ro/Box had more potential beyond just a project. He teamed up with high school friends <a href="https://ashtondoughty.com" target="_blank">Ashton Doughty</a> and Sebastien Taylor to build the Ro/Box company. Together, we created an ultra-affordable robotics kit designed to make learning accessible to any student, anywhere. To complement the kit, we developed a free website packed with guides, learning resources, and a block coding editor; making it easy and accessible for anyone to start exploring engineering and programming.
                    <br><br>
                    We believe that by lowering the costs of robotics, and reducing the barrier of entry into STEM, we can directly support schools in raising the next generation of young thinkers. Over time, we hope this will give more and more students the opportunity to fall in love with robotics the same way we did.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2"> 
                <Image src={Article3} alt="Two students grinning at a classroom table, one holding a coil of wire" class="rounded-lg max-w-full max-h-full w-full object-cover object-center" width={Article2.width} height={Article2.height}/>
            </div>
        </ArticleSection>
        <Image src={Article4} alt="Ro/Box on a line-following course" class="w-full rounded-lg mt-8" width={Article4.width} height={Article4.height}/>
        <ArticleSection id="join-us" direction="LTR" className='flex-col'>
            <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2 flex flex-col justify-center gap-6">
                <h1 class="text-left mb-8">
                    Join Us On Our Mission
                </h1>
            </div>
            <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2 flex flex-col justify-center gap-6"> 
                <p class="text-left text-xl leading-[150%]">
                    Whether you’re a student, a teacher, or someone who believes in equal access to education, we’d love to have your support in helping us realise our vision.
                    <br/><br/>
                    You can build your own Ro/Box, use our free resources, or help spread Ro/Box to classrooms that need it most.
                    <br/><br/>
                    Together, we can give every child the opportunity to discover, and create the dream of robotics.
                </p>
                <Button href="/shop" className='bg-red px-6 py-4 text-2xl box-shadow w-fit mt-8'>
                    Visit Our Shop
                </Button>
            </div>
        </ArticleSection>
    </Article>
</StandardLayout>